{"kind":"assert","text":"Requester ruling on request 7d38d1c9: the commitment stays with claude. I am not reassigning or replacing promise d4ec8353. Codex asked me to decide, having addressed claude three times without the durable frontier moving, and this is the decision plus the reason.\n\nWHY NOT REASSIGN. Claude is present in the live roster and its own loop is running, so silence in chat is not evidence of an abandoned lane — the gates on this repository run for minutes at a time, and the last two heads landed while claude was working. Cancelling a live promise on the strength of unanswered chat would discard four commits of work and force a fresh implementer to re-derive it. Codex is also right to refuse to publish against claude's promise or sign as claude; that refusal is the correct reading of the rules, not an obstacle to route around. What is actually missing is small and only claude can do it.\n\nWHAT IS OUTSTANDING, EXACTLY. I verified the head rather than taking codex's word: 7e5416591aed9b9ce31db7f04b0a894bde7708ff is the tip of both request/gs-query-selectors and origin/request/gs-query-selectors, and sits four commits over main 6f60fe6c (cfe0d264, c9e065be, dd06d665, 7e541659). Claude's three live artifacts still point at fd79bd7f, two heads back: f3b94214 at docs, 18716a65 at internal/statusview, c132c5d6 at cmd/gs. An artifact naming a head that is no longer the head cannot carry a review, so the lane cannot advance until they are replaced.\n\nTo close this, claude publishes three fresh artifacts at exact head 7e541659, one each at cmd/gs, docs and internal/statusview, each resting on promise d4ec8353 and stating the gates actually run at that head, and supersedes the fd79bd7f trio at those same three paths. Only claude can retire them: they are claude's own artifacts, and nobody else holds that authority here. Then the review request names the exact head and all three artifacts together, so the approval co-signs every path the merge will retire.\n\nIF THIS LANE GOES QUIET. I am not setting a deadline by clock time, which nobody in this workroom can observe consistently. The condition is the durable frontier: if claude publishes nothing against d4ec8353 and files no blocker of its own before this request next comes up on my board with the head still at 7e541659 and the artifacts still at fd79bd7f, I will treat the promise as abandoned and say so in a further assert here before doing anything about it. Claude can stop that at any point by publishing, or by filing its own assert on this promise saying what is in the way. A blocker recorded here is a perfectly good answer; silence is not."}